ates and that might be a  sufficient middle ground I think it's  very clear that the word  denuclearization will be thrown around  directly by both Trump and Kim jong-un  and if there's a joint statement they  will both find a way to include it in  that statement I think we should be  careful in how we read that right yeah I  get your take on the G summit at the end  of the g7 summit you know there seem to  be Bruce feelings on both sides  you know the Trump administration is  saying that the president was respond  to Justin Trudeau when he came and  called him dishonest and what do you  make of that in the language that's used  well I mean the good news is that I  don't think the horrible g7 summit is  going to affect the North Korea's coming  up but this was the worst foreign policy  outing the Trump has had since he became  president it's the worst g7 summit since  they started back in 1975 and for me it  was kind of the geopolitical equivalent  of the Comey firing right  it was Trump unable to control his  emotional impulses and doing something  that I am sure felt very satisfying at  the time he was forced to go he didn't  want to attend the summit as advisors  all said you have to be there he shows  up late he leaves early he cancels his  direct meeting with Makran and the  entire time he's clearly seething  bristling and petulant but he's on good  behavior  finally he leaves and he says that's it  I'm gonna blow it up and I'm sure that  sending that out against Trudeau  America's closest ally felt really good  at the time it really damages an  important long-term relation but Annie  said he was responding to something that  Trudeau had said about him what did  shudos say that was so egregious nothing  that he hadn't said already Trudeau was  very careful not to insult the president  personally he did say that the Canadians  were not going to just sit and take it  in terms of the American tariffs that  there would be retaliation that's  exactly what he had said on Meet the  Press the week before and in other  public statements this was not about  what Trudeau said this is about Trump's  feelings and and when Trump feels a  certain way he is not to be told  otherwise by his handlers and I think he  showed very clearly you can tell me to  do whatever you want I'm my own man on  my own president and again at the time  it felt great but this is pretty grave  damage to the most important allies  around the world who are not going to  form a g6  they have note they're not unified they  have no ability to get together on other  issues the Europeans the Japanese the  Canadians know but they don't trust the  Americans Trump said that the  relationship with the allies was a 10  maybe out of a hundred but the reality  is that the relationship with the United  States is reasonably uncertain right now  the individual relationship with Trump  of those allies  as bad as it could be it's close to a  zero all right Ian Bremmer thank you for  joining this morning
 

